00:38:46,620 --> 00:38:48,200
that they find aesthetic or beautiful

892
00:38:48,200 --> 00:38:51,400
or informative or memorable or interesting?

893
00:38:51,400 --> 00:38:53,640
So we're going to take a generative model

894
00:38:53,640 --> 00:38:56,800
and tune it to make outputs-- an image-generative model

895
00:38:56,800 --> 00:39:00,040
and tune it to make outputs that humans rate

896
00:39:00,040 --> 00:39:02,360
as being more desirable images?

897
00:39:06,360 --> 00:39:11,400
So let's look at how you can do this search over

898
00:39:11,400 --> 00:39:13,985
through the space of generative outputs

899
00:39:13,985 --> 00:39:15,360
using a scoring function, but not

900
00:39:15,360 --> 00:39:18,560
with an autoregressive model, but now with an image generator.

901
00:39:18,560 --> 00:39:20,560
And it's going to be the type of image generator

902
00:39:20,560 --> 00:39:24,360
that has latent variables, z, and maps z through g of z

903
00:39:24,360 --> 00:39:25,500
to an output image.

904
00:39:25,500 --> 00:39:28,680
So that could be a GAN or the decoder of a VAE,

905
00:39:28,680 --> 00:39:32,160
or it could be a diffusion model where z is the noise.

906
00:39:32,160 --> 00:39:34,520
And I'll come to the question in a second.

907
00:39:34,520 --> 00:39:38,080
So we're also going to have a scoring function, which

908
00:39:38,080 --> 00:39:42,730
will, in this case, be derived from CLIP as just an example.

909
00:39:42,730 --> 00:39:45,350
So it's going to be an encoder for an image

910
00:39:45,350 --> 00:39:46,730
and an encoder for text.

911
00:39:46,730 --> 00:39:50,310
And the score will be, how well does the image match the text/

912
00:39:50,310 --> 00:39:53,470
So the text input is, what is the answer to the ultimate

913
00:39:53,470 --> 00:39:55,837
question of life, the universe, and everything?

914
00:39:55,837 --> 00:39:57,670
I'm going to try to maximize the dot product

915
00:39:57,670 --> 00:40:01,110
between the text and the image.

916
00:40:01,110 --> 00:40:02,590
The image encoder and text encoder

917
00:40:02,590 --> 00:40:04,798
are pre-trained with the CLIP objective, so remember,

918
00:40:04,798 --> 00:40:07,830
that will try to make it so that the caption that

919
00:40:07,830 --> 00:40:11,577
matches an image will have the maximal dot product.

920
00:40:11,577 --> 00:40:13,410
So this is basically going to try to search.

921
00:40:13,410 --> 00:40:16,227
If I search over the space, z, optimize over z,

922
00:40:16,227 --> 00:40:18,310
I'm going to search over the latent variables that

923
00:40:18,310 --> 00:40:21,750
will create an image that matches this text according

924
00:40:21,750 --> 00:40:23,470
to the CLIP model.

925
00:40:23,470 --> 00:40:26,130
So this is kind of constrained optimization.

926
00:40:26,130 --> 00:40:28,730
I'm not searching over the space of all possible pixels.

927
00:40:28,730 --> 00:40:30,217
I'm using my image generator.

928
00:40:30,217 --> 00:40:32,050
I'm only searching through the latent space.

929
00:40:32,050 --> 00:40:34,110
So I'm only going to be making outputs

930
00:40:34,110 --> 00:40:37,390
that are high-probability under the generative models

931
00:40:37,390 --> 00:40:40,170
distribution, as long as I'm constraining z

932
00:40:40,170 --> 00:40:42,230
to be high prior probability.

933
00:40:42,230 --> 00:40:44,870
Remember that things like VAEs have a prior over z,

934
00:40:44,870 --> 00:40:45,670
which is Gaussian.

935
00:40:45,670 --> 00:40:49,010
So if I just search over the high-probability part

936
00:40:49,010 --> 00:40:50,930
of the unit Gaussian, maybe I just search over

937
00:40:50,930 --> 00:40:52,915
the unit hypersphere, then I'm going

938
00:40:52,915 --> 00:40:54,290
to be staying within the manifold

939
00:40:54,290 --> 00:40:56,850
of high-probability images according to the image

940
00:40:56,850 --> 00:41:01,210
generator, and I'll find the one that matches this text

941
00:41:01,210 --> 00:41:07,570
So here's what that looks like So this

942
00:41:07,570 --> 00:41:10,890
was-- the first batch of text-to-image generative models

943
00:41:10,890 --> 00:41:13,930
that were really impressive were of this kind.

944
00:41:13,930 --> 00:41:16,190
This method is called CLIP + VQGAN.

